s; do echo \"== $p\"; dotnet test tests/DcaShop.$p 2>&1 | grep -E \"Bestanden|Fehler!|error\" | tail -3; done; echo \"== format\"; dotnet format --verify-no-changes; echo \"exit $?\"","timeout":600000,"description":"Run unit, integration, architecture, e2e tests and format check"}}],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"is_error":false,"num_turns":19,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"The catalogue page's title now reads \"Product Catalog\", and the story's browser test passes.\n\n**The change:** one line in `src/DcaShop.Web/Views/Product/Catalog.cshtml:2`. The title was \"Products\" and is now \"Product Catalog\". The heading \"Our Products\" and the breadcrumb \"Home / Products\" stay as they are, as decision CAT-01-01 answered.\n\n**Checks:** all green.\n\n| Check | Result |\n| --- | --- |\n| Build | 0 errors |\n| Unit tests | 176 passed, 4 skipped |\n| Integration tests | 63 passed, 1 skipped |\n| Browser tests | 39 passed, 1 skipped |\n| Architecture rules | 129 of 129 passed |\n| Formatter | no changes; it touched no other file |\n\n- **Build file:** written to `tasks/catalogue-title/build.md`. It records no deviations from the plan.\n- **Architecture guard:** I applied `dca-discipline` to the view; the change adds no import and no domain or cross-context reference.\n- **Not used:** the build carrier `dca-modelling`, because there was no domain type to build, and the knowledge catalog `dca-knowledge`, because nothing architectural needed deciding.\n\n**Still open:** the test's name, \"The catalogue page is titled \\\"Product Catalog\\\"\", has to appear as a scenario in `../dca-sample-specification/scenarios.md`. A test with the same name also has to exist in the Java suite. Without both, the check that matches tests to scenarios will fail when it runs with the specification switched on. That sync work is outside this story.\n\nI ran no other stage and committed nothing.","ttft_ms":3143,"type":"result","duration_ms":120784,"uuid":"c88e43b7-cac1-4e35-baaf-fbb8b9c3fa59","ttft_stream_ms":2279,"time_to_request_ms":32,"first_content_frame_ms":2280,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
